  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "NEW\n\t\t\t* Invocation counts everywhere: a wasInvoked: argument (a Moq.Times) on expression, named-method and whole-service verification.\n\t\t\t* ValueTask: When/Having/Until and mocked members take it like Task. No more .AsTask().\n\t\t\t* Dictionaries and strings keep their vocabulary when chaining: dict.Has().Count(2).and.Key(\"a\").\n\t\t\t* Failures report what TSpec had to work around, under a WARNINGS section.\n\n\t\t\tCHANGED\n\t\t\t* Enum generation varies instead of always yielding the first member. Mentions vary but are not unique — the docs overstated this.\n\t\t\t* IsInt, IsByte, ... are now IsIntegral<T> / IsNullableIntegral<T>. Assertions unchanged.\n\t\t\t* For.None is rejected with a clear SetupFailed wherever a scope is given, instead of failing obscurely later.\n\n\t\t\tBREAKING\n\t\t\t* An async lambda, or one that is a bare throw, must state its return type: When(async Task<int> (_) => ...). Otherwise Task and ValueTask are ambiguous.\n\t\t\t* Write Has().Order() — Has().Order<int>() is gone.\n\t\t\t* Deprecated: the Then/And<TService>().WasInvoked(Times) continuation.\n\t\t\t* Binary-breaking: HasEnumerable gained a type parameter. Recompile.",
